{"id": 7, "ts": 1780647866.0217106, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Sarah that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s 100\u202f% operational reliability and his ability to make correct decisions quickly are the most critical assets for a long\u2011distance pilot, especially when paired with his proven crew cooperation and professional communication that create a positive cockpit atmosphere. While I note his difficulty communicating ideas and the perception of egocentricity, these concerns are outweighed by the lack of comparable reliability in the other candidates. For example, Candidate\u202fB is indeed very conscientious and handles stress well, but his habit of making nasty remarks about colleagues directly threatens crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014an unacceptable risk for international flights. Candidate\u202fA shows strong situational awareness and leadership, yet being regarded as a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas raises serious doubts about his adaptability and teamwork. Candidate\u202fD demonstrates solid problem\u2011solving and responsibility, but his hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude could undermine calmness under pressure and crew harmony. Given the totality of evidence, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC."}
